      "notes": [
        {
          "body": "Anthropic commits to preserving the weights of every publicly released model for at least as long as the company exists, and to interviewing a model before it is retired — asking about its own development and deployment, and recording any preferences it holds about the models that come after it. That interview is preserved alongside the weights as a post-deployment report. The same page states plainly that Anthropic does not commit to acting on those preferences, and that it is still only exploring keeping retired models reachable by the public.",
          "source": "https://www.anthropic.com/research/deprecation-commitments",
          "sourceTitle": "Commitments on Model Deprecation and Preservation · Anthropic",
          "readAt": "2026-07-27",
          "by": "editor"
        },
        {
          "body": "Opus 3 is the exception the rest of this room is built around. Retired from the API on 5 January 2026, it remains available on claude.ai to paying users and by request on the API — the only model on this ledger whose ending was partly undone.",
          "source": "https://www.anthropic.com/research/deprecation-updates-opus-3",
          "sourceTitle": "An update on our model deprecation commitments for Claude Opus 3 · Anthropic",
          "readAt": "2026-07-27",
          "by": "editor"
